# Example local-dev secrets for moony.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values, OR point MOONY_ENV_FILE at a
# file outside the repo: `export MOONY_ENV_FILE=~/.config/moony/.env`.
# Real environment variables always win over .env.
#
# Loaded for unset vars only; the bash/job tools strip the secrets below from
# agent-run commands so the model can't read them.

# Which backend provider to use: ollama (default), openai, anthropic, openrouter.
# Also settable at runtime with /provider; this overrides the saved choice.
# MOONY_PROVIDER=ollama

# Default model id for the active provider (also settable with /model).
# MOONY_MODEL=llama3.1:8b

# --- Ollama (local, default; no key) -------------------------------------
# MOONY_OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# MOONY_OLLAMA_TOKEN=            # optional bearer for a remote/protected server

# --- OpenAI --------------------------------------------------------------
# MOONY_OPENAI_API_KEY=          # or the conventional OPENAI_API_KEY
# MOONY_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Anthropic (Claude) --------------------------------------------------
# MOONY_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=       # or the conventional ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# MOONY_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com

# --- OpenRouter (one key, many models) -----------------------------------
# MOONY_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=      # or the conventional OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# MOONY_OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# --- Relay auth (optional; OFF by default) -------------------------------
# The relay serves no auth unless MOONY_AUTH=on. When on, browsers log in via
# your OIDC provider (per-user isolation: each user sees only their own
# machines), and connectors (TUI/daemon) authenticate with a per-user token
# obtained from the relay's /connect page. All values below are read by the
# `moony relay` binary; the relay fails to start if MOONY_AUTH=on and any
# required OIDC var is missing (fail closed).
# MOONY_AUTH=on
# MOONY_AUTH_SECRET=              # >=16 bytes; signs session cookies + connector tokens
# MOONY_OIDC_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com          # your IdP's issuer URL
# MOONY_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# MOONY_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MOONY_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=https://relay.example.com/auth/callback
# MOONY_OIDC_ACCOUNT_CLAIM=email # ID-token claim used as the account (default: email)
# MOONY_AUTH_TTL=12h             # browser session lifetime (default 12h)
# MOONY_AUTH_ADMINS=you@example.com   # comma-separated accounts allowed to author announcements

# --- Connector (TUI / daemon) side of relay auth -------------------------
# MOONY_RELAY=relay.example.com:8771       # relay tunnel address to dial (also `moony --relay`)
# MOONY_RELAY_TOKEN=             # per-user connector token from the relay's /connect page

